        "spiritualArchitecture": "The architecture of Jwala Ji is a spectacular display of the Indo-Sikh and hill styles. The temple features a massive golden dome and spires that shine across the valley. A unique feature is the inner sanctum which is a natural rock-cut chamber where the nine flames emerge from the crevices. The architecture is designed to lead the pilgrim into the intimate presence of the fire, with the heat and the light being the primary experience. The use of silver-plated doors and the intricate marble work in the courtyard create a sense of a royal and divine court. The complex includes several smaller shrines and a sacred tank where the water is said to boil without heat.",
