    'Sacred Destination', 
    'uk', 
    'The "Guardian of the Char Dham", Dhari Devi is located on the banks of the Alaknanda river near Srinagar in Uttarakhand. It is a site of absolute protective authority and ancient Himalayan power, where the upper half of the Goddess Sati is believed to have fallen, representing the watchful presence of the Mother who protects the mountain valleys from the floods of the heavens.', 
