    'uk', 
    'The "Varanasi of Kumaon", Bageshwar is an ancient town located at the confluence of the Sarayu and Gomti rivers. It is a site of absolute Shaiva authority and ancient Vedic history, where the Lord Shiva is worshipped as Bagnath (the Tiger Lord), representing the absolute lordship over the nature and the sacred gateway to the higher Himalayan reaches.', 
    '560.2', 
