) VALUES -- [REMOVED LEGACY DUPLICATE] (
    'Surkanda Devi (Dhanaulti)', 
    'surkanda-devi-temple', 
    'Sacred Destination', 
    'uk', 
    'Perched at an altitude of 2,756 meters, Surkanda Devi is one of the most significant Shakti Peethas in the Garhwal Himalayas. It is a site of absolute panoramic authority and divine protection, where the head of Sati is believed to have fallen, representing the absolute peak of the spiritual shield that guards the Mussoorie-Chamba ridges.', 
    '450.5', 
